# The natural numbers, the first counting structure: the distinctions counted, zero and a successor for each. Their
# arithmetic is addition (repeated successor) and multiplication (repeated addition). Counting the distinctions gives
# the naturals, and ordering them, then signing them, gives the integers, the unique totally ordered rung whose
# one-way order is the arrow of time. This is the first object Vibe Theory rests on.

# The additive laws below hold for EVERY natural (the parameters are universally quantified), proved by the linear
# prover and checked by `seed test`. These are universal laws, not single witnesses.

# Zero is a right identity for addition: n + 0 = n, for every n.
rule zero-is-right-identity-for-addition
  seat n, like natural
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call add
        read n
        code 0
      read n

# Addition commutes: a + b = b + a, for every a and b.
rule addition-commutes
  seat a, like natural
  seat b, like natural
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call add
        read a
        read b
      call add
        read b
        read a

# Addition associates: (a + b) + c = a + (b + c), for every a, b, c.
rule addition-associates
  seat a, like natural
  seat b, like natural
  seat c, like natural
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call add
        call add
          read a
          read b
        read c
      call add
        read a
        call add
          read b
          read c

# Every natural is non-negative: n >= 0, for every n. This is the base of the order, the floor the arrow runs up from.
# (The `natural-number` refinement is what carries the n >= 0 assumption to the prover.)
rule every-natural-is-at-least-zero
  seat n, like natural-number
  show hold
    call is-minimum
      read n
      code 0

# Multiplication distributes over addition: a (b + c) = a b + a c, for EVERY a, b, c. A universal law (not a witness),
# proved by the commutative-ring normalizer. With commutativity and associativity of addition above, this makes the
# naturals a commutative semiring, the algebraic floor the integers and the whole tower are built on.
rule multiplication-distributes-over-addition
  seat a, like natural
  seat b, like natural
  seat c, like natural
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call multiply
        read a
        call add
          read b
          read c
      call add
        call multiply
          read a
          read b
        call multiply
          read a
          read c

# Multiplication commutes: a b = b a, for every a and b. The semiring is commutative.
rule multiplication-commutes
  seat a, like natural
  seat b, like natural
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call multiply
        read a
        read b
      call multiply
        read b
        read a

# Multiplication associates: (a b) c = a (b c), for every a, b, c.
rule multiplication-associates
  seat a, like natural
  seat b, like natural
  seat c, like natural
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call multiply
        call multiply
          read a
          read b
        read c
      call multiply
        read a
        call multiply
          read b
          read c

# The inductive summation identities (the triangular numbers, the sum of odds, squares, and cubes), each a closed form
# proved for every n by Peano induction, live in the sum file.
